Z||000003||Pontiaddict||08-21-2001||01:06 AM||||Do you prefer power? (As in a v8) or economy? (a v6 swap)<BR>Auto or 5 speed?<BR>Any other options on the car? (not really needed, just wondering  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)<BR>I wouldn't suggest doing the fastback conversion but it's a matter of preferance.<P>Look around ans list all the engine conversions you are thinking of and we'll hepl you decide. Or we'll start a flame war trying to.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Steve Normington||08-21-2001||11:02 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pilrulz:<BR><B>cost not major problem<BR>medium mechanical ability<BR>DIY<BR>would be cool to have a sleeper i can use as a daily driver (must have power to back up looks)</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>As I see it, you have three options:<BR><A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com" TARGET=_blank>Small Block Chevy</A><BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/fierov6/OSG/mod.3800-V6.html" TARGET=_blank>3800 SC</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html" TARGET=_blank>Cadillac 4.9/Northstar</A><P>Personally, I'd go for the SBC with Archie's kit because my current engine swap has been a major headache and I'd want a complete, bolt-in kit if I do this again. In addition to the engine, you are going to want to upgrade the brakes and suspension.<P>PS. What are the local laws regarding emissions for your car?<p>[This message has been edited by Steve Normington (edited 08-21-2001).]||||reg||1
